# Schema and type safety

**Binding:** [ADR-008: Schema-led domain contracts](../adrs/ADR-008-schema-led-domain-contracts.md) (Accepted). **AI validation:** [ADR-007](../adrs/ADR-007-ai-provider-contract.md). **Module layout:** [`src/lib/api/README.md`](../src/lib/api/README.md).

## Zod and inference

- **Source of truth:** Zod schemas for persisted domain rows, HTTP API bodies/responses under `src/routes/api/**`, validated Supabase/sync/AI JSON, and any structure serialized to IndexedDB or the wire (ADR-008).
- **Types:** Use `z.infer<typeof Schema>` (or equivalent from composed schemas). **Do not** hand-duplicate the same field contract in a parallel `interface` / `type` for those entities.
- **Boundaries:** Validate user input, **network JSON** (including **OpenAI** and **Supabase** responses where the app asserts shape), and model output with **`.safeParse()`** (or transforms) before treating values as domain types; avoid unchecked casts at trust boundaries (ADR-008 §7; overlaps deprecated AI paths in [`docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md`](../docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md) **GAP-006**).

## Where types live

| Situation | Placement |
| --------- | --------- |
| Domain entities, API envelopes, AI structured shapes, auth/session/permission **logic** | `src/lib/api/<domain>/`: **`*.schemas.ts`** (Zod), **`*.types.ts`** (inferred re-exports and rare type-only helpers that **do not** duplicate entity fields), **`*.model.ts`**, **`*.service.ts`**, **`index.ts`** — see [`src/lib/api/README.md`](../src/lib/api/README.md). **Do not** place these in `$lib/utils`. |
| Dexie `Table<>` entities and rows | Types imported from the **owning domain barrel** (`$lib/api/...`); **new tables** get a Zod schema in that domain before widening generics (ADR-008 §4). |
| **Generic** or **cross-cutting** contracts reused across many non-Svelte modules (e.g. shared layout data, feature-flag shapes) | `src/lib/types.ts` (or a dedicated module under `src/lib/` if size warrants) — **not** a second home for recipe/suggestion/preferences/etc. that already belong under `$lib/api/**`. |
| **Domain-agnostic** pure helpers (date parse, secure random bytes, generic string casing) with no owning API domain | `src/lib/utils/<name>.ts` — see [`src/lib/utils/README.md`](../src/lib/utils/README.md). **Not** a catch-all; when a domain exists, use `$lib/api/<domain>/`. |
| Single-file type aliases | Colocate with the implementation when they are not imported elsewhere. |

## Svelte components

- **`.svelte` files** are not modules for shared exports. Do **not** define **shared** domain or app-wide interfaces in `.svelte` only to reuse them across files; move them to **`$lib/types`** (cross-cutting) or **`$lib/api/<domain>`** (domain).

## Strict object schemas

- New or materially revised **object** schemas under `src/lib/api/**` should use **`.strict()`** (or equivalent) so unknown keys fail validation (ADR-008 §6). When tightening legacy schemas, prefer incremental updates in the same change that touches the schema.

## Transforms and composition

- **Transforms:** Prefer schema **`.transform()`** (and related Zod coercion helpers) at validation boundaries instead of mutating parsed objects with ad hoc logic—keeps invariants and errors in one place.
- **Composite schemas:** Model structured entities (e.g. suggestion payloads, full vs saved recipe shapes) by **composing** smaller schemas (`merge`, `extend`, shared bases under `api/common`) rather than copy-pasting fields.
- **Persisted vs transient:** Make it obvious in naming, module split, or short comments which parts of a domain are **durable Dexie rows**, **HTTP-only envelopes**, or **ephemeral AI output**—ADR-008 exclusions still apply for purely ephemeral structs.

## OpenAI Responses structured output (`zodTextFormat`)

- Schemas passed to **`zodTextFormat`** (see [`src/lib/api/ai/ai.model.ts`](../src/lib/api/ai/ai.model.ts)) must stay **JSON-schema-friendly**: straightforward object and array shapes and primitives; use **`.describe()`** (and similar) for model guidance.
- **Do not** rely on **`.transform()`**, **`.pipe()`**, or non-trivial **`.refine()`** on that **same** Zod object—the Responses + Zod integration does not handle them well. **Normalize** in a **second** schema or `safeParse` **after** the structured response is valid ([ADR-007](../adrs/ADR-007-ai-provider-contract.md) structured response contract).

## Example (object schema + inferred type)

```ts
export const RecipeSchema = z
	.object({
		id: z.string().uuid(),
		title: z.string(),
		ingredients: z.array(z.string()),
		steps: z.array(z.string())
	})
	.strict();

export type Recipe = z.infer<typeof RecipeSchema>;
```

Use **`.safeParse()`** on `RecipeSchema` (or composed schemas) for user input, network JSON, and model output before treating values as `Recipe`.

## Imports

- Prefer **`import type`** for type-only imports to avoid accidental runtime cycles and unnecessary bundle edges.
- Prefer consuming domain types from **`$lib/api/<domain>`** barrels rather than legacy parallel paths (ADR-008 *Implementation compliance*; deprecated duplicates in `$lib/types` are being retired in a separate code pass).

## Escalation

- Conflicts with Accepted ADRs or intentional contract drift: [`.cursor/rules/adr-compliance.mdc`](./adr-compliance.mdc) and [`docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md`](../docs/readme-adr-alignment-gaps.md).
